{"id": "clm:bcf615171b631b6cf5f9754983f3fcbffb04ce7f4b418af1da73d57f1e811d22", "type": "statement", "text": "A server-selection timeout means the driver could not select a suitable server within its selection budget. Investigate topology and underlying exceptions; the headline alone does not establish a network outage. Read preference and server eligibility also affect selection. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/server-selection/server-selection.md", "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0883544e490339e0f45e5e4f9ecc5e436b8bc4cd2b575ae2c443fec291a52782", "ev:67128037b49bbd006f43f5788a6d2677bfeb2f71435a0a8e01ea6b185641fe35", "ev:da3398cd9f75fa181eb640d25bb6bd79642894399a47f6eb2473347793965970"]}
{"id": "clm:246284a275de47ba56371826cdb23920e0093a8d13ab066585ee1aa9d7152dec", "type": "statement", "text": "A Mongoose buffered-operation timeout can occur when a model belongs to an unconnected connection, even if another connection succeeded. Verify the model's connection and await it; disabling bufferCommands can expose missing connection setup. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/faq.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4f8c0aa505aef4546f408c162333a70d409ca966f6007a2cb762645efc3d6811", "ev:851ae9133282c4be392770ef53d6803251db7d8e0841778bd1f7a5b1bb6e1401", "ev:c09fd2d81ec34edcf55315711fdee7e4712b84ac65260c513c9cb8664e9fd325"]}
{"id": "clm:4b855416d1431919815e4e7d4a150bc52aae6aeb2d4d39dfebb005132aa53cdd", "type": "statement", "text": "Mongoose buffers model calls before connection. When operations appear to hang, check connection initialization and model binding; disabling bufferCommands can expose connection mistakes. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4f8c0aa505aef4546f408c162333a70d409ca966f6007a2cb762645efc3d6811", "ev:c09fd2d81ec34edcf55315711fdee7e4712b84ac65260c513c9cb8664e9fd325"]}
{"id": "clm:f49d2ff36039d20c955786e2950d886fdf042932e8b1ef7df841ca688fa1940a", "type": "statement", "text": "Troubleshooting must distinguish server error codes from client connection failures: the server code reference interprets mongod/mongos errors, while Mongoose also exposes driver server-selection failures and model-operation buffering failures. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/error-codes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4f8c0aa505aef4546f408c162333a70d409ca966f6007a2cb762645efc3d6811", "ev:903628af0995a24208df9828c029d1ba223f696859d7b4a50f5e9e4e8664b36e", "ev:da3398cd9f75fa181eb640d25bb6bd79642894399a47f6eb2473347793965970"]}
{"id": "clm:2385b5e3d9e9552066dbb043f604ede1c93f802d49345428c203d312958596a7", "type": "statement", "text": "In Mongoose, inspect the error reason and reason.servers descriptions. A replica-set member advertising localhost can produce ECONNREFUSED even when the application URI uses remote hostnames; inspect rs.conf() member addresses. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:da3398cd9f75fa181eb640d25bb6bd79642894399a47f6eb2473347793965970"]}
{"id": "clm:c1c1c615246235b9b9ab37fe4ebe7fc0f4d7b92890f40465b73ae7f1c9690f1a", "type": "statement", "text": "Collect the complete exception and stack trace, credentials-redacted connection string, driver and server versions, DNS lookup output, connectivity tests, and relevant logs before escalating a server-selection failure. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f6b1d841e25b12cd9eb74d8c248a7ead920a41098cc547a2090676bc06a9dc40"]}
{"id": "clm:de3b019ac997be0eced62219b028d86498479acbb2096f95f0bcfc9bc3dda4ac", "type": "statement", "text": "The retryable-writes specification uses RetryableWriteError labels to determine retryability. Matching an arbitrary exception message or retrying every server error is not an equivalent implementation of this protocol. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:499de6e850b3dd6604cea50212745a854aa43c10edf158316a9c903290e55ff1", "ev:4eb748e24775dae4955c4be2fca1f4257d9fef7b175f15258cf3a2c3e858bf9e", "ev:b08aa9f807cc0cab2604ba34ef5947b1c40bf3d35decb9502993fe978d0474c7"]}
{"id": "clm:8235cd2c88a5e87682add1a24933ebbaffc19a2330f15a32a43754f50f4184c4", "type": "statement", "text": "The retry budget depends on timeout configuration: ordinary retryable writes allow one retry, while client-side operation timeout through timeoutMS can permit additional attempts until success, a non-retryable error, or budget expiry. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/retryable-writes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4eb748e24775dae4955c4be2fca1f4257d9fef7b175f15258cf3a2c3e858bf9e", "ev:78fdbed788a0ae6d67a5c2281040ce63b14e27dbec1a491f7ec6deecd55c49c1"]}
{"id": "clm:4a42280dc8cacfc5f00d48a86982ddd6bbad082179c4aa56e94384ae13f31215", "type": "statement", "text": "NoWritesPerformed indicates no write was performed. MongoDB documents this label beginning in 6.1; the driver specification also preserves an error indicating a write attempt when later failures are known no-ops, so final-error handling must retain outcome uncertainty. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/retryable-writes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:250754a6b113c3c6e344182b764d3c47db09798bff1b14f9d6ac1aa3324eaa81", "ev:de5ea8547cdf5ff0443b9d636a4d931e5ca27cd4b4626ec84891e29ac07d0565"]}
{"id": "clm:bdf7cfafb5179a6c141d1b14d6bc062a17a0abc760109b9757b87efb8e0210c0", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB distinguishes Unauthorized (13), AuthenticationFailed (18), MaxTimeMSExpired (50), WriteConflict (112), NotWritablePrimary (10107), and DuplicateKey (11000). Preserve the numeric code and symbolic name when classifying a failure; these identify different error categories. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/error-codes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/base/error_codes.yml"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1368b78a5eb93d4932a48bb08513da155d3951df24ef9425adf65ef4fe82df54", "ev:37197e1cefad7c44ad9393d52f03496f2517b1f4d7e97f759effb9fb2e773bda", "ev:65fe411832929082314905dde4a3809de5881607e607cf235d1661689996e792", "ev:d8c0be52449d2697882124abc3b8ec838a599c90040d79e97b07dd43cdfd7d77", "ev:e559f8c9f36a748d73c990507ae0232eb2f71246f0dc43c6bcfbc085d6eaa480", "ev:eba8e663107222fe0ea486e4217738f85aebd1a1762bcdd8d7ad45ce62f638ce"]}
{"id": "clm:99e68c86392bfeb353041ea20e7b4159aa2745b54e6903eb26af45c97136bf93", "type": "statement", "text": "Mongoose initial connection failure rejects mongoose.connect(); handle that promise with catch or try/catch. After connection, observe error and disconnected events. An error event alone does not cover every loss of connectivity. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:af0f7251102a4aa03df00be3311e4124d96b00d7ad706c8b800ec61bf2976660"]}
{"id": "clm:c8fe9b5ae1e92217a8d0eddcb4248c4339f37e1b30b29f2e92f12c394c4ed34d", "type": "statement", "text": "Starting with MongoDB 6.1, NoWritesPerformed can establish that a failed retryable write performed no writes. Preserve partial bulk results and error context; a generic failure or absence of that label does not establish that nothing changed. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/retryable-writes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1bc3603f7fb96509ba273e595c7d3e0fc5b687545022b65fe516a3a2ef86ec86", "ev:250754a6b113c3c6e344182b764d3c47db09798bff1b14f9d6ac1aa3324eaa81", "ev:de5ea8547cdf5ff0443b9d636a4d931e5ca27cd4b4626ec84891e29ac07d0565"]}
{"id": "clm:eab56e4fc5b06d43e0683c599bd6665c41d422ee4fb5e6232b6beb883bc29c28", "type": "statement", "text": "Server-selection timeouts mean the driver could not find a suitable server in time. Investigate nested errors and topology information alongside deployment availability, network rules, DNS, TLS, and authentication rather than treating the timeout alone as a root cause. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b62d79ace0b60f10802bd2d966412f9256d8dc2ca4e27e01a1906f431abc9b7c", "ev:da3398cd9f75fa181eb640d25bb6bd79642894399a47f6eb2473347793965970"]}
{"id": "clm:358fab498c2a8e9a96e95735d1db9bde4b3a5c625ad453fa8edda44fcc51fc40", "type": "statement", "text": "DuplicateKey (11000) indicates a violated unique index. Diagnose the indexed fields and rejected values rather than assuming every duplicate-key error concerns _id. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/base/error_codes.yml", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-unique/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1368b78a5eb93d4932a48bb08513da155d3951df24ef9425adf65ef4fe82df54", "ev:6327230a8d2d45358399bbb3284ee25be91d061a25650c23f3720e9fd59caa2a", "ev:661b119a42a9a9bb14bce97a6fb03e8e54abaf2052afd2da8348845d1051be19"]}
{"id": "clm:4633e35baa9fa3ba076a3817458f39c0999d88bdfd480404069126ed85008791", "type": "statement", "text": "Use driver retry eligibility and error labels rather than retrying every exception. MongoDB retryable-write execution preserves its session/transaction identity; an application issuing a fresh write does not automatically preserve that identity. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1bc3603f7fb96509ba273e595c7d3e0fc5b687545022b65fe516a3a2ef86ec86", "ev:4eb748e24775dae4955c4be2fca1f4257d9fef7b175f15258cf3a2c3e858bf9e", "ev:b08aa9f807cc0cab2604ba34ef5947b1c40bf3d35decb9502993fe978d0474c7", "ev:b0c588be1a630b6b8ce141d536b392561214e2abd63aabc8a937745539fd94c7", "ev:f4234b1e18745eab34ebbed31dd09b8ee8cca5454bf56d1b43b72255ad9ed81e"]}
{"id": "clm:caf55cbb673e745ce7ab50a1bed560ed626764ba804427a1668a6dede9aa1518", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's source definitions map 13 to Unauthorized, 18 to AuthenticationFailed, 50 to MaxTimeMSExpired, 112 to WriteConflict, 121 to DocumentValidationFailure, and 11000 to DuplicateKey. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/base/error_codes.yml", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1368b78a5eb93d4932a48bb08513da155d3951df24ef9425adf65ef4fe82df54", "ev:27cc1c763437e434ba931c2e07cb78903fb4d791480b4f3f8da91d266018306b", "ev:37197e1cefad7c44ad9393d52f03496f2517b1f4d7e97f759effb9fb2e773bda", "ev:65fe411832929082314905dde4a3809de5881607e607cf235d1661689996e792", "ev:d8c0be52449d2697882124abc3b8ec838a599c90040d79e97b07dd43cdfd7d77", "ev:e559f8c9f36a748d73c990507ae0232eb2f71246f0dc43c6bcfbc085d6eaa480"]}
{"id": "clm:947438606b3c986edb7c3603a796d608470fc61a8ae5704ebf9a38bb3a02e11b", "type": "statement", "text": "For duplicate-key failures, inspect the actual unique index. Mongoose's unique schema option requests an index; it does not itself enforce uniqueness before the index exists. Tests that recreate a database can await Model.init() before asserting duplicate rejection. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/faq.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/base/error_codes.yml", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-unique/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:df66d7cf1b5127e40169be8f9f75dd1b972fcdba3152c9c7386240f8ad1a5bb3"]}
{"id": "clm:4e7da2b62056393f01e0a0a86ae179585d7d1b5a17c17e52eb521951fc796ab8", "type": "statement", "text": "For local connections refused at ::1:27017, Mongoose documents an IPv6 localhost mismatch. Using 127.0.0.1 or enabling server IPv6 support addresses that specific configuration problem. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/connections.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/Automattic/mongoose/blob/master/docs/faq.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bc1129643b1f081fa3bf9ce0fb8a7831faf592af601b57cd203561708b1a40db"]}
{"id": "clm:b1487c376fac7091eb673de3de5a1d3e2f52ad422aa1c8272bed151b5722f965", "type": "statement", "text": "For mongodb+srv DNS failures, run nslookup -type=SRV _mongodb._tcp.<cluster-name>.mongodb.net from the application host. Verify the hostname, returned records, DNS provider support, and outbound DNS access before changing connection settings. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d03cb4a2485c95c6bc855c0d30d2cc9aeb58ac353f8920066aac83389fa117e9"]}
{"id": "clm:12eb1849ffd277886e740d3cfae5681ad20b64c299b757f52c93f28f0a4dcb88", "type": "statement", "text": "Retryable writes require an eligible deployment and acknowledged operations. Standalones, unacknowledged writes, and multi-document updateMany/deleteMany operations do not receive ordinary retryable-write protection; transaction statements are not individually retryable. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/retryable-writes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:21a8a956094e8fae33468662f74f6e2bf95585e0d6810cc3106c148abc9c50c2", "ev:b904c9ac0a38bdf55b166112af3bfa8c7d71fc76ae7c35b3058e5a3ce07af287"]}
{"id": "clm:8d2c36651f4f5ae13dfc0bd20461558b4e62db9c97ede582f98a4c5325fd5b9f", "type": "statement", "text": "Application-level re-execution of a write needs idempotency analysis. AWS's DocumentDB example shows repeated $inc changing a counter repeatedly, while MongoDB's retryable-write protocol reuses the transaction identity to provide at-most-once execution; those are different retry mechanisms. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/building-resilient-applications-with-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility-part-2-exception-handling/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1bc3603f7fb96509ba273e595c7d3e0fc5b687545022b65fe516a3a2ef86ec86", "ev:905c0c662d3702ed1e1fdb38be4e07335a6ed72d59ab31fe74da74ad20d95f73", "ev:a1d7c2d8fe2572198f1a2616a6fbdd9fd219c3d4cdfbb733e097d89c593ec5d6"]}
{"id": "clm:8723f25c0644a2ac43226f1c15d945eb392d89e30a14b45a496c54e12ebee3fb", "type": "statement", "text": "Elastic issue 4541 reports an instrumentation bug in APM Java agent 1.55.1/1.56.0: closing a cached shared JAR could kill MongoDB monitor class loading, leaving the client CONNECTING and ending in MongoTimeoutException. The issue includes ZipFile closed and NoClassDefFoundError traces and a maintainer-confirmed fix, providing a concrete non-network timeout diagnosis. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/elastic/apm-agent-java/issues/4541", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0292b76ed94a390b193e77f5a54110ee6baf44639c5f6523cadb091360fbacbb", "ev:9bd9f0ee5345980cbd343e2bb06624ff95c44c79612c69ef5ae6fabfda407190"]}
{"id": "clm:ea9a8cb4aaf238dce85c1cb4bf41387f75330354bd76246b11101b3c4793a377", "type": "statement", "text": "For connection diagnosis, check deployment availability, outbound TCP access, Atlas IP access rules, DNS SRV resolution, and TLS certificate configuration. Correlate driver discovery logs with incoming-connection evidence in server logs. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/troubleshooting/server-selection-timeout/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8c0584f873cce0cc834ee50769af6b002b37d2fc5e7b39576bfef1596c793fe0"]}
{"id": "clm:a801f03b7d64c769349d5f7093c8bcef1e7a70fc3aa59561812c8ac66df6851c", "type": "statement", "text": "An ordinary unique single-field index treats missing and explicit null values as a null index key, permitting only one such entry. A unique partial index constrains only documents matching its filter; choose that filter to reflect the intended optional-field semantics. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-unique/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ab045850afbfbef71644a947d2a88a26a06fd38e15a544cf77e10e0b7cf2e8a"]}
{"id": "clm:8deb9c2edbf0b2c8ad8ade2e3c3b6d6ce02c9acb958650c7b46a075a1c0c132a", "type": "statement", "text": "Retryable writes require an eligible replica-set or sharded deployment and acknowledged writes; standalone deployments and w:0 writes do not qualify. Writes inside a transaction are not individually retried by retryWrites. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/retryable-writes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/retryable-writes/retryable-writes.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:21a8a956094e8fae33468662f74f6e2bf95585e0d6810cc3106c148abc9c50c2"]}
{"id": "clm:abe3482243015e76bdf9d539b92dc66538e6994c1a5cb4d08ce44ce280a1acbc", "type": "statement", "text": "AWS DocumentDB exception-handling guidance illustrates a general application-retry hazard: a lost response can leave the write outcome unknown, and issuing a fresh non-idempotent increment may apply it twice. Its sample mitigation uses operation identifiers and conditional updates; this is DocumentDB guidance, not proof of MongoDB server behavior. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/building-resilient-applications-with-amazon-documentdb-with-mongodb-compatibility-part-2-exception-handling/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Error Codes and Troubleshooting"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:63765da10c9676265daa80789e357c65608d0a0de0c7e6bb54b1ebc463358d28", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5f375bfe203c855cb1629e4f695d9af356e8bf5442eecd865f075f6e9d2b41ca", "ev:905c0c662d3702ed1e1fdb38be4e07335a6ed72d59ab31fe74da74ad20d95f73", "ev:d9e923b6eaeeec7ecdfa60d91dec9bc7aee1c813f7b27acb3643046c8448ad63"]}
